  "title": "Builder-family detection and diff-aware review posting",
  "summary": "This change makes two parts of the review pipeline stricter and more honest. Builder-family detection now reads every word of a `Code-Generator:` trailer (so `Anthropic Claude Code claude-sonnet-5-5` and `Claude Sonnet 5.5` both resolve to `anthropic`), refuses to guess when words point at two families, and fails the whole run closed as could-not-run when any commit has no trailer — except a clean merge, which `git merge-tree --write-tree` proves introduces nothing of its own. Separately, review posting now fetches the PR diff and only places inline comments on lines the diff actually shows; findings outside it move into the body, which is cut to the 2000-byte limit and counts what did not fit instead of refusing to post.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
